d measured, estimated, or unavailable, and a missing value is stored as unknown, never as zero.\"\n292-      verify: \"1) Find where context size is recorded. 2) Check a label of measured, estimated, or unavailable, and how missing values are stored. 3) Answer no if there is no label, or a missing value defaults to `0` (`or 0`, `?? 0`, `.get(..., 0)`).\"\n293:    - id: R07.3\n294-      check: \"The count comes from a stated method that handles cached input and compaction, not a copied per-call billing total.\"\n295-      verify: \"1) Find how context size is counted. 2) Check a stated method covers cached input and compaction. 3) Answer no if it copies `usage.input_tokens` or a billing total with no stated method that matches it, or ignores cache and compaction.\"\n296:    - id: R07.4\n297-      check: \"The value is carried across tool handoffs and stored with the action's identity, result, and trace ID.\"\n298-      verify: \"1) Trace context size through tool handoffs and sub-agent calls. 2) Check it is stored with action identity, result, and trace ID. 3) Answer no if it is lost on handoff, or stored separately with no link to the action.\"\n299-  not_covered:\n300-    - problem: \"Behavior not compared across context-size ranges\"\n301-      owner: R09\n302-    - problem: \"Token or cost limits not enforced outside the model\"\n303-      owner: B07\n304-    - problem: \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\"\n305-      owner: A02\n306-\n307-R08:\n308-  provable_from_code: partly\n309-  look_for:\n310-    - \"Security detection rules kept apart from answer-quality evals, for example SIEM rules, Falco rules, or alert definitions in the repo.\"\n311-    - \"Rules for encoded payloads, unexpected outbound traffic, out-of-scope writes, privilege escalation, and repeated denied calls.\"\n312-    - \"Denials and policy decisions emitted as events that rules can match.\"\n313-    - \"Alert routing to a named responder (for example PagerDuty or Opsgenie